                        "entry_id": "dd77acc5-064b-361a-86cf-aa2ae11e57c1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "That purls; rippling, eddying."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b146cf7e-a2df-42c0-ac27-01ba48a9de9c",
                                "sense_id": "e61b1a9e-e438-39f1-a065-487f9abbbc69",
                                "text": "[Thomas Jefferson] was up near the source of the River of America, near the Three Forks, while we are downstream from New Orleans in a broad, deep, incredibly powerful river that often feels more like a sewer than a purling mountain stream."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6def328b-5bd9-4471-97c1-fa5bc2d980da",
                                "sense_id": "e61b1a9e-e438-39f1-a065-487f9abbbc69",
                                "text": "They have sometimes caused an high steepy mountaine to arise in the midst of the sayd Amphitheaters, all over-spred with fruitfull and flourishing trees of all sortes, on the top whereof gushed out streames of water as from out the source of a purling spring."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "31c8ee28-5b05-4ec4-a511-20b6bfa0f9eb",
                                "sense_id": "e61b1a9e-e438-39f1-a065-487f9abbbc69",
                                "text": "\"Thank Heaven,\" cried Henrietta, laughing, \"you do not, even in fancy, turn me into a shepherdess, with sheep on one side, and a purling brook on the other.\""
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
